Module pans "The cold pans" {
  Description "The salt-pans of {town} burn fuel day and night, and Iscoed has no wood to spare. {trader}'s fuel boat from {fuelvillage} is two days late. If the fires under the pans are out three days, the brine spoils and the season's salt with it.".
  Entity party: group "Your company".
  Place town "The town" is settlement.
  Place shop "The salt-house" is room.
  Place green "The green" is room.
  Place fuelvillage "The fuel village" is settlement.
  Place fuelgreen "The green at the fuel village" is room.
  Entity trader: group "The salter".
  Relation fuelled(group). Relation spoiled(group). Relation hired(group). Relation paid(group). Relation asked(group).
  Relation carted(group). Relation shared(group). Relation laidoff(group).
  // The boat poled off the staithe and going down the cut with the company: the company's own journey to the town,
  // walked on the map, brings her in (TR-20: the act had put the company in the boiling-house, hexes off, with no
  // journey and no map; an act is never the way into another hex).
  Relation afloat(group).

  Entity cold: fact "{trader}'s salt-pans at {town} are going cold: the fuel boat from {fuelvillage} is two days late, and the brine spoils if the fires are out three days.".
  Initially Assert established(cold).
  Entity boatman: fact "The fuel boat is at {fuelvillage}'s staithe, full: Ianto, its boatman, has broken his arm.".
  Entity work: fact "{trader} pays a hand three coin a shift to rake salt and keep the fires at the pans.".
  // The cut is the sea-gate's cut (ST-04; mission-22/story-sheets.md, the cold pans' sheet): the sea up it since the
  // pawl's pin was sawn, and Gatesend's eel-men running their boats up it at night. Shut, it runs out clean at the ebb
  // (cut_clear: the gate's module, installed after this one, teaches it as the gate is wound shut); what came of the
  // boat is the salt in the reeve's tally and a fuel boat seen on the eel-men's water (the gate's, which reads these).
  Entity cut_clear: fact "With the sea-gate at Gatesend shut, the sea is off the sluice-cut, and it runs out clean at the ebb.".
  Entity poled: fact "You poled Ianto's fuel boat down the sluice-cut by daylight, where Gatesend's eel-men run their boats at night.".
  Entity salt_whole: fact "The fuel boat's whole load went to {trader}'s pans, and Ffion Wyn's stayed cold.".
  Entity salt_shared: fact "The fuel boat's load was shared, two parts to {trader}'s pans and a third to Ffion Wyn's.".
  Entity salt_lost: fact "{trader}'s brine spoiled for want of fuel, and the season's salt with it.".

  Kind fuel_sack_kind "a sack of charcoal" is gear worth 1 weighing 20 described "A sack of charcoal from the ridge, black to the touch and lighter than it looks, tied at the neck with a twist of reed.".
  Place boiling "the boiling-house behind the salt-house" is room within town at 5, 5.
  Passage boiling_door "the door to the boiling-house" is door between shop and boiling.
  Place staithe "the staithe at {fuelvillage}" is room within fuelvillage at 3, 6.
  Passage staithe_lane "the lane down to the staithe" is passage between fuelgreen and staithe.
  Item sacks "two sacks of charcoal" is fuel_sack_kind at staithe.

  // The one chimney is a lead, not the aim (HP-01): the boat is an aim once {trader} is asked why the pans are cold
  // (trader_cold), and the lead's knowing is let go then.
  Entity chimney: fact "Only one chimney smokes over the salt-houses at {town}, and {trader} watches the river for the fuel boat from {fuelvillage}, two days late. {trader} is at the salt-house.".
  Initially Assert askedOf(chimney, trader).
  Observe cold_sign at green as sign when not fuelled(party) and not spoiled(party) and not knows(party, cold) and not knows(party, chimney) "Over the salt-houses only one chimney is smoking, thin and grey. A salter stands in a doorway with his arms folded, looking up the river for the fuel boat from {fuelvillage}, two days late." teaches chimney.
  Observe boiling_cold at boiling when not fuelled(party) and not spoiled(party) "Three iron pans the size of a cart-floor stand over brick hearths, the brine in them grey and still. Only one hearth is lit, low, fed with broken barrel-staves. A crust of salt is setting on the cold ones like ice.".
  Observe boiling_hot at boiling when fuelled(party) "All three hearths roar. The brine seethes in the pans and the air is thick with steam and the smell of the sea, and a man with a long wooden rake draws the white salt up onto the boards to drain.".
  Observe boiling_spoiled at boiling when spoiled(party) "The pans are cold and the brine in them has gone to a brown scum. Two men are tipping it out into the ditch, and nobody is speaking.".
  Observe staithe_scene at staithe when not fuelled(party) "A flat-bottomed fuel boat lies tied up at the staithe, sacks of charcoal heaped in her waist. On the bank a man sits with his arm strapped across his chest, looking at her.".
  Observe ianto_says at staithe as sign when not fuelled(party) and not knows(party, boatman) "'Broke it on the windlass, loading her,' Ianto calls up to you, and lifts the strapped arm. 'She's full. I can't pole her down one-handed, and nobody here will take her through the cut.'" teaches boatman.
  Person ianto "Ianto" at staithe { Role "the fuel boatman of {fuelvillage}, with a broken arm". Pronouns he. Peaceable. Manner grim. }

  Topic trader_cold with trader "Ask {trader} why the pans are cold" when toldMatter(trader, actor) and not fuelled(party) and not spoiled(party) once {
    Says "{trader} wipes salt off both hands. 'No fuel. The boat from {fuelvillage} is two days late and there's not a stick to be had in {town}: the ridge wood is the reeve's and the peat is wet. Three days cold and the brine's spoiled, and the season with it.' A look at your arms. 'If you've a back, I'll pay for it. Get me fuel and there's work here after.'".
    On discuss { Assert asked(actor). Assert knows(actor, cold). Retract knows(actor, chimney). }
  }
  Topic ianto_boat with ianto "Ask Ianto about the fuel boat" when not fuelled(party) once {
    Says "'Broke it on the windlass, loading her,' says Ianto, and nods at the arm. 'She's full. Two sacks would keep his fires a day or two; the whole load, a month. I can't pole her down with one arm, and nobody here will take her through the sluice-cut since the water went wrong.' He looks at you. 'You could carry two. Or pole her, if you've done it.'".
    On discuss { Assert knows(actor, boatman). }
  }
  // Why nobody at the staithe will take her through: they have been told not to (the sheet's opposing claim).
  Topic ianto_cut with ianto "Ask Ianto why nobody will take her through the cut" when knows(actor, boatman) and not fuelled(party) and not knows(actor, cut_clear) once {
    Says "'Since the sea-gate at Gatesend went, the sea comes up the cut on every tide, and the eel-men with it,' says Ianto. 'They run their boats up it at night, and they don't care for a boat on it by day. Ifan Rhys came up this staithe at the new moon and said so, civil as you like.' He spits into the river. 'Nobody here has crossed Ifan Rhys yet. And the silt's bad where the sea comes in.'".
  }
  Topic ianto_shut with ianto "Ask Ianto why nobody will take her through the cut" when knows(actor, boatman) and not fuelled(party) and knows(actor, cut_clear) once {
    Says "'The eel-men of Gatesend, that run the cut at night,' says Ianto. 'Ifan Rhys said a boat on it by day was a boat that saw things.' He looks down the river. 'But they say the sea-gate's shut again. Then the sea's off the cut, and she'll go down clean at the ebb, with nobody's boats on it to see.'".
  }
  // Poled down, the whole load comes to the pans; carried, two sacks and a day's walk.
  Action pole_boat(actor: group, site: place) "Pole Ianto's fuel boat down the cut to {town}" {
    Speaker ianto. Time 1 hour.
    Requires able(actor) and company(actor) and at(actor, site) and at(actor, staithe) and knows(actor, boatman)
      and not fuelled(actor) and not spoiled(actor) and not carted(actor) and not afloat(actor)
      and not knows(actor, cut_clear).
    Resolve check(actor, brawn, dc_fair).
    On success { Assert afloat(actor). Assert knows(actor, poled). }
    On failure { Assert carted(actor). }
    Result "The boat is heavy and the cut is half-silted below the staithe where the sluice has let the sea in, and twice you ground her on the mud and lever her off with the pole. Then she is clear, low in the water and going down with the ebb, and {town} is the rest of the way down the cut.".
    Otherwise "Where the old sluice has let the sea into the cut, the boat goes hard aground on the mud and will not come off. You leave her there, and Ianto shakes his head. Two sacks will still go, carried.".
  }
  // With the sea-gate shut the sea is off the cut, and the boat comes down it without grounding (the sheet's handoff
  // in from the gate: shut, the cut is passable; open, it grounds).
  Action pole_shut(actor: group, site: place) "Pole Ianto's fuel boat down the cut to {town}" {
    Speaker ianto. Time 1 hour.
    Requires able(actor) and company(actor) and at(actor, site) and at(actor, staithe) and knows(actor, boatman)
      and not fuelled(actor) and not spoiled(actor) and not carted(actor) and not afloat(actor)
      and knows(actor, cut_clear).
    Result "With the sea-gate at Gatesend shut, the sea is off the cut, and at the ebb the water runs out of it clean and brown over the silt. The boat is heavy, but she does not ground once below the staithe, and she goes down with the ebb toward {town}. A man mending a trap on the bank at Gatesend will watch you all the way past.".
    On success { Assert afloat(actor). Assert knows(actor, poled). }
  }
  // Come down to the town with her, by the company's own journey: the boat at the quay, and the salter to be told.
  Rule boat_in when afloat(party) and within(party, town) says "Ianto's fuel boat noses into {town}'s quay, low in the water, and men come running from the salt-house." {
    Retract afloat(party). Assert carted(party). }
  Action give_sacks(actor: group, site: place) "Give {trader} the charcoal" {
    Speaker trader. Time 10 minutes.
    Requires able(actor) and company(actor) and at(actor, site) and at(actor, shop) and holding(actor, fuel_sack_kind) and not fuelled(party) and not spoiled(party).
    Result "{trader} has the sacks open before they are off your back, and the fires in the boiling-house going within the hour. 'Two days,' {trader} says, 'and the boat after, Ianto or no Ianto.' Eight coin on the boards. 'There's three a shift for you here, whenever you want it.'".
    On success { Spend fuel_sack_kind from actor. Assert fuelled(actor). Increase quantity(actor, gold) by 8. Assert knows(actor, work). Assert knows(actor, salt_whole). }
  }
  Action boat_come(actor: group, site: place) "Tell {trader} the fuel boat is at the quay" {
    Speaker trader. Time 10 minutes.
    Requires able(actor) and company(actor) and at(actor, site) and at(actor, shop) and carted(actor) and not fuelled(party) and not spoiled(party).
    Result "{trader} goes out onto the quay and stands looking at the heaped boat for a long moment. 'The whole load,' {trader} says. 'A month.' Fifteen coin on the boards, slowly. 'There's three a shift for you here, whenever you want it. And I'll remember it.'".
    On success { Assert fuelled(actor). Assert paid(actor). Increase quantity(actor, gold) by 15. Assert knows(actor, work). Assert knows(actor, salt_whole). }
  }
  // A second claim on the boat (the owner's structural critique, 18 November, and mission-22/story-sheets.md, the cold
  // pans' sheet: the salter, the boatman and the village had all wanted the same thing, and the boat was a delivery).
  // Ffion's pans stand cold beside the salter's, and Ianto has always sold to the bigger man first: the whole load is
  // the salter's season and her rakers laid off, a third of it two smaller seasons and the salter's grudge.
  Person ffion "Ffion Wyn" at green { Role "a salter of {town}, whose pans stand cold beside {trader}'s". Pronouns she. Peaceable. Manner grim. }
  Entity ffion_need: fact "Ffion Wyn's pans at {town} are cold too, and the fuel boat has always gone to {trader} first; she would pay a fair price for a third of it.".
  Topic ffion_cold with ffion "Ask Ffion about her pans" when not fuelled(party) and not spoiled(party) once {
    Says "'Cold as {trader}'s, and colder,' says Ffion. 'When the boat comes, the boat is his. Ianto has always sold to him first: he's the bigger man, and pays on the nail.' She looks up the quay at her own dead chimney. 'My rakers have had nothing since the feast. Two days more and I let them go. If a third of that load came my way, I'd give a fair price for it.'".
    On discuss { Assert knows(actor, ffion_need). }
  }
  Rule rakers_off when not fuelled(party) and not spoiled(party) and not laidoff(party) and watch(clock) >= 216 says "Ffion Wyn has laid off her rakers. They stand on the quay in a knot, owed since the feast, watching the river for a boat." { Assert laidoff(party). }
  Action share_load(actor: group, site: place) "Tell {trader} the fuel boat is at the quay, and that a third of it is Ffion's" {
    Speaker trader. Time 10 minutes.
    Requires able(actor) and company(actor) and at(actor, site) and at(actor, shop) and carted(actor) and knows(actor, ffion_need) and not fuelled(party) and not spoiled(party).
    Result "{trader} goes out onto the quay and looks at the heaped boat, and then along it at Ffion's cold chimney, and for a long moment says nothing. 'A third,' {trader} says. 'You're free with my fuel.' Ten coin on the boards, not fifteen, and no word of work after. By evening two chimneys are smoking over the salt-houses.".
    On success { Assert fuelled(actor). Assert paid(actor). Assert shared(actor). Increase quantity(actor, gold) by 10. Assert knows(actor, salt_shared). }
  }
  Topic ffion_shared with ffion "Ask Ffion how her pans go" when shared(party) once {
    Says "'Burning,' says Ffion, 'and my rakers back at them, and paid.' She counts four coin into your hand. 'For the third. {trader} won't forget it, and nor will I.'".
    On discuss { Increase quantity(actor, gold) by 4. }
  }
  Topic ffion_left with ffion "Ask Ffion how her pans go" when fuelled(party) and not shared(party) once {
    Says "'Cold,' says Ffion. 'The boat came, and it went to {trader}, as it always does. My rakers have gone up the river road to look for work.' She does not look at you.".
  }
  Observe pans_shared at green when shared(party) "Over the salt-houses two chimneys are smoking, and Ffion's rakers are on the quay with their rakes over their shoulders.".
  Observe pans_whole at green when fuelled(party) and not shared(party) and knows(party, ffion_need) "Over the salt-houses {trader}'s chimneys are smoking. The pans beside them are cold, and nobody stands at Ffion's door.".
  // An ordinary livelihood: a shift at the pans, paid, once the fires are lit by one the salter will hire (not one who
  // gave a third of his fuel away).
  Action shift(actor: group, site: place) "Work a shift at the pans for {trader}" {
    Time 8 hours.
    Requires able(actor) and company(actor) and at(actor, site) and at(actor, boiling) and fuelled(actor) and knows(actor, work) and not dark().
    Result "You rake salt until your shoulders burn and feed the hearths until your face does, and at the end of it {trader} counts three coin into your hand without a word.".
    On success { Increase quantity(actor, gold) by 3. Assert hired(actor). }
  }
  Rule spoils when not fuelled(party) and not spoiled(party) and watch(clock) >= 432 says "Word comes up from the waterfront: {trader}'s fires are out, and the brine in the pans has spoiled. There will be no salt from {trader}'s pans this season." teaches salt_lost {
    Assert spoiled(party). Assert stale(cold).
  }
  Milestone m_fuelled "kept {trader}'s pans burning" worth 100 when fuelled(party).
  Objective cold_aim when knows(party, cold) and not knows(party, boatman) and not fuelled(party) and not spoiled(party) toward ianto "Find out what has become of {trader}'s fuel boat at {fuelvillage}: the salt-pans at {town} go cold in three days without it.".
  Objective cold_fetch when knows(party, boatman) and not fuelled(party) and not spoiled(party) and not carted(party) and not afloat(party) toward ianto by staithe "Bring {trader} fuel from Ianto's boat at {fuelvillage}: pole her down the cut, or carry two sacks.".
  Objective cold_carry when holding(party, fuel_sack_kind) and not fuelled(party) and not spoiled(party) toward trader by boiling "Take the charcoal to {trader}'s boiling-house at {town}.".
  Objective cold_down when afloat(party) and not carted(party) and not fuelled(party) and not spoiled(party) toward trader by shop "Bring Ianto's fuel boat down the cut to {trader}'s salt-house at {town}.".
  Objective cold_told when carted(party) and not fuelled(party) and not spoiled(party) toward trader by shop "Tell {trader} in the salt-house that the fuel boat is at the quay.".
  Rule word_old when fuelled(party) and not stale(cold) { Assert stale(cold). }
  // The boat at the staithe is over once it has left it, and Ffion's want once the fuel has gone where it went
  // (FH-25: the Notes had kept both after the pans were lit).
  Rule boat_old when (afloat(party) or carted(party) or fuelled(party) or spoiled(party)) and not stale(boatman) { Assert stale(boatman). }
  Rule ffion_old when (fuelled(party) or spoiled(party)) and not stale(ffion_need) { Assert stale(ffion_need). }
  Goal fuelled(party).
}
